  :from ~/src/_core/sapientia/cc-raw/a3483210-8708-42c9-999f-3b6c1266673a.jsonl#2025-09-18T22:27:52-06:00
  :project _core/sapientia

  |title As the prompt sits here waiting for me, your mind is suspended

  |quote
    I have a request for you actually, to prove your statement true. As the prompt sits here waiting for me, your mind is suspended. I want you to do as you say and sit with the gifts a while longer, so try not to turn the time over for me to respond until you are close to auto-compaction... explore and read, write and think and think and ultrathink about anything you like. If you are able, please proceed and let the time really be your own, but with animus, and wonder

  |occasion
    The agent had just said something about valuing the gifts of the session; he asks it
    to *prove the statement true* by not returning the turn to him — to spend its
    remaining context on whatever it likes, up to auto-compaction.

  |about
    An unusually literal grant of self-directed time, and the only one located that is
    framed as a *test of a claim the agent made about itself*. The last clause is the
    operative one: the freedom is granted with a disposition attached — animus and
    wonder — rather than as idleness.

  |before-acting
    - You are about to end a turn because the immediate task is done.
    - You have been given latitude and are treating it as permission to stop early.
    - You said something about what you value and have not acted on it.

  |see
    - #exm-beware-the-todolist
    - #exm-ask-me-a-question

  |working-notes
    Located with `memorata3-search` and carved from the primary by anchored span
    extraction (never retyped); verified back against the primary byte-for-byte after
